1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,680
How many party balloons would it take

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:03,120
to lift you into the sky?

3
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:05,520
A balloon floats because helium is lighter

4
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:07,120
than the air it pushes aside.

5
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:09,040
But one balloon only lifts about ten

6
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:09,840
grams,

7
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:11,360
about as much as two coins.

8
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:12,960
A grown-up weighs around seventy

9
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:13,760
kilograms.

10
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:15,440
So you'd need roughly seven thousand

11
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,160
balloons,

12
00:00:16,160 --> 00:00:17,840
a bunch bigger than a bus.

13
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:18,880
And as you rise,

14
00:00:18,880 --> 00:00:20,880
the air gets thinner and colder,

15
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,720
and the balloons swell until they start

16
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:23,360
to pop.

17
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:24,800
In 1982,

18
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,960
a man tied about forty weather balloons

19
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:28,000
to a lawn chair.

20
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,240
He floated nearly five kilometres up,

21
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:31,520
cold and scared,

22
00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:33,120
and came down by popping them,

23
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:34,080
one by one.

24
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:34,640
So yes,

25
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,920
balloons can lift you.

26
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:38,308
Getting down is the hard part.
